From: Artur Andrzejczak <andrzejczak.artur@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 19 Sep 2026 09:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drm/amdgpu: poll the fence fallback timer at 2 ms (BC-250 probe, not a fix)

On the BC-250 (gfx1013) SDMA fence trap interrupts were not being delivered
under the July 2026 stack, so ring fences completed only through the fallback
timer, and with AMDGPU_FENCE_JIFFIES_TIMEOUT at HZ/2 the KFD map/unmap storm of
a model load took about thirty minutes. This probe polls at 2 ms instead.

Kept for the record and not recommended: the rebuilt module did not speed the
load, the wait turned out to be HSA-signal-level, not kernel fence
timeout, and the loading problem was later resolved by the TLB flush changes
and the navi12 SDMA microcode (INVESTIGATION.md in the repository).

Written with the help of Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic) under the author's
direction; the author built and tested it on the board.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Artur Andrzejczak <andrzejczak.artur@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu.h
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu.h
@@ -278 +278,4 @@
-#define AMDGPU_FENCE_JIFFIES_TIMEOUT		(HZ / 2)
+/* BC-250 (gfx1013 Cyan Skillfish): SDMA fence trap interrupts are not delivered
+ * on this board, so ring fences only complete via this fallback timer. HZ/2
+ * (500ms) makes KFD map/unmap during model loading take ~30 min. Poll at 2ms. */
+#define AMDGPU_FENCE_JIFFIES_TIMEOUT		(HZ / 500)
